  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">InfraCo Asia/InfraCo Africa Investments provide mezzanine and equity finance for infrastructure projects in South Asia, South East Asia and Africa to bridge the gap if an absence of capital is likely to delay the project.</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This activity InfraCo Asia/InfraCo Africa Investments provide mezzanine and equity finance for infrastructure projects in South Asia, South East Asia and Africa to bridge the gap if an absence of capital is likely to delay the project. is a component of PIDG2 - Second phase of FCDO&apos;s Support to the Private Infrastructure Development Group .  reported by FCDO with a funding type of 109 - Multilateral organisation and a budget of &#xa3;149,036,621. This project benefits Developing countries, unspecified. It works in the following sector(s): Energy generation, non-renewable sources, unspecified, Information and communication technology (ICT), Transport policy and administrative management, Low-cost housing, Sanitation - large systems, Agricultural services.</narrative>
  </description>
